 "note": "Cartoon picture-book Petite École seen from its yard (same building as on the village square: white walls, giant open book for a roof, slate roof edge, little bell turret on the left). Every room has its own sign: six coloured ground-floor doors, each leading straight into its room (left to right: L'alphabet A–M yellow, L'alphabet N–Z mint, Les nombres blue, Les articles lavender, Les questions peach, Les pronoms green); five first-floor windows with coloured shutters and signs (Grands nombres teal, Pronoms 2 red, Prépositions 1 lime, Prépositions 2 blue, Conjonctions lilac), reached by the indoor stairs from the pronouns hall; two attic dormers (Pronoms 3, Prépositions 3) reached by the stairs from the conjunctions room. The cobbled path at the bottom left goes back to the square.",
